6. EXCEPTION FOR PLUGINS AND EXTENSIONS

6.1 Plugins and extensions that do not implement authentication or
authorization and do not run in the authentication IAM (the "Extension
Plugins") may be distributed under the license of their choice, including
proprietary, commercial or closed source.

6.2 This exception does not apply to:
• plugins, adapters or modules that implement authentication or
  authorization (including IAM IdP adapters);
• any component that embeds, copies or derives from the Software.

6.3 Extension Plugins must:
• interact with the Software only through the documented plugin API and the
  signed manifest;
• not impose on the Software or its users any terms incompatible with this
  License (in particular, not require the Software to be distributed under
  the plugin's license, nor claim ownership of the Software);
• preserve the Software's notices and not use its trademarks without
  permission.

6.4 The Software remains governed by this License; the exception does not
waive the Initial Licensor's rights in the Software.

